            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F001:F005\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Claim C0000 correctly captures the manufacturer's remedy obligations under paragraph (1) (F001:F003). Paragraph (2) (F005) establishes separate rules—a prima facie evidentiary presumption, Secretarial authority to extend the 60-day period, and a rule defining qualifying presentation—which are already independently represented by existing claims C0001, C0002, and C0003. Appending paragraph (2) to the summary and context of C0000 conflates distinct provisions, creates duplicate content across claims, and does not fix a defect.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F001:F005\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Under F003, the remedy of refunding the purchase price less depreciation is expressly limited to vehicles ('(B) for a vehicle, refund the purchase price...'). The proposal alters this substantive rule by stating that refund is available 'for either a vehicle or replacement equipment', directly contradicting the source text. Additionally, it inappropriately incorporates paragraph (2) into C0000.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
